BES-NET supported:
Sea-grass pollination research;
Establishment of butterfly gardens and pollinator displays in the Botanical Gardens of Trinidad as well as Tobago;
Testing of honey at various aviaries throughout Trinidad & Tobago to assist in the development of a quality standard for stingless bee honey;
Bat pollination research;
Development of pollinator protocols;
Development of local plants and pollinators database;
Development of a Theory of Change for a Pollinator Conservation Strategy;
Drafting of guidelines for the management of stingless bees;
Design and implementation of a public awareness campaign on pollinators and pollination

GEF SGP supported: 
Conduct pollinator surveys in North East Trinidad and Tobago; 
Research study to identify types of bee species in Trinidad & Tobago;
Pollinator workshops

