Establish a GBV hotline where survivors of violence are moved along a continuum of care to access appropriate medical and
psychosocial support services including: 
(A) Counselling (Psychologist) - for survivors of violence, those at risk of experiencing
violence and those who have experienced trauma because of violence; 
(B) Case Management; 
(C) Emergency Contraception and
other critical interventions within the Clinical Management of Rape package; 
(D) Contraceptives information and commodities;
(E)Doctor's Consultation; 
(F) Registered Nurse (RN) Consultation/Counselling; 
(G) Outbound/Extremal Referrals. When needed, survivors will be offered Dignity kits.
